[00:04.48] I hear the drizzle of the rain
[00:14.25] Like a memory, it falls
[00:19.44] Soft and warm, continuing
[00:25.67] Tapping on my roof and walls
[00:30.77] And from the shelter of my mind
[00:38.85] Through the window of my eyes
[00:44.46] I gaze beyond the rain drenched streets
[00:49.86] To England where my heart lies
[00:59.95] My mind's distracted and diffused
[01:10.46] My thoughts are many miles away
[01:16.52] They lie with you when you're asleep
[01:21.59] And kiss you when you start your day
[01:28.03] And a song I was writing is left undone
[01:36.35] I don't know why I spend my time
[01:41.44] Writing songs I can't believe
[01:47.48] With words that tear and strain to rhyme
[01:53.23] And so you see I have come to doubt
[02:06.02] All that I once held as true
[02:11.24] I stand alone without beliefs
[02:17.41] The only truth I know is you
[02:23.69] And as I watch the drops of rain
[02:31.47] Weave their weary paths and die
[02:37.62] I know that I am like the rain
[02:42.33] There but for the grace of you go I
